:: Home_Kitchen [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<div class="map-here">📍 Home → Kitchen</div>
<h1>The <span class="accent">Kitchen</span></h1>

<div class="prose-block">
<p>A kitchenette, really, counter, stovetop, a cabinet above it with eleven ramen packets standing between you and a very bad month. The microwave died three weeks ago. The single chair at the tiny table has one leg shorter than the others.</p>
</div>

<div class="action-list">

<<link '<span class="action-icon">☕</span><span class="action-text">Make instant coffee<span class="action-sub">Bitter, but it works.</span></span>' "Home_Kitchen">>
	<<set $player.energy to Math.clamp($player.energy + 5, 0, 100)>>
	<<set $player.stress to Math.clamp($player.stress - 2, 0, 100)>>
<</link>>

<<if $day is 0>>
	<<if not $ateBreakfast>>
		<<link '<span class="action-icon">🥣</span><span class="action-text">Eat breakfast<span class="action-sub">Stale cereal, expired milk, and your phone.</span></span>' "Home_Kitchen_Breakfast">><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<p class="text3 small">You already ate. Your stomach isn&apos;t impressed, but it&apos;s quiet for now.</p>
	<</if>>
<<elseif $day is 1 and $novaCureDay1Done>>
	<<if not $ateDinnerDay1>>
		<<link '<span class="action-icon">🍜</span><span class="action-text">Eat something<span class="action-sub">Leftover ramen. Cold, from the cup.</span></span>' "D01_EveningHome">><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<p class="text3 small">You&apos;re not hungry anymore. You&apos;re not much of anything anymore.</p>
	<</if>>
<<elseif $day is 2 and $d02Ate>>
	<p class="text3 small">Pizza&apos;s gone. You&apos;re full, for once.</p>
<</if>>

<<link '<span class="action-icon">🥤</span><span class="action-text">Drink some water<span class="action-sub">Free, at least.</span></span>' "Home_Kitchen">>
	<<set $player.stress to Math.clamp($player.stress - 1, 0, 100)>>
<</link>>

<<if $day is 2 and $cookingSkill is 0>>
	<<link '<span class="action-icon">🍝</span><span class="action-text">Cook something<span class="action-sub">Try actual pasta, not just ramen</span></span>' "Home_Kitchen_CookD2">><</link>>
<<elseif $knowsBeanSoupRecipe>>
	<<link '<span class="action-icon">🍲</span><span class="action-text">Make Hector&apos;s bean soup<span class="action-sub">Cheaper than ramen, tastes like God&apos;s kitchen</span></span>' "Home_Kitchen">>
		<<set $player.energy to Math.clamp($player.energy + 35, 0, 100)>>
		<<set $player.stress to Math.clamp($player.stress - 3, 0, 100)>>
	<</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link '<span class="action-icon">🍜</span><span class="action-text">Cook something<span class="action-sub">Instant ramen, cereal, or eggs, whatever&apos;s in the cabinet</span></span>' "Home_Kitchen">>
		<<set $player.energy to Math.clamp($player.energy + 20, 0, 100)>>
	<</link>>
<</if>>

<<if ($timeslot is "Evening" or $timeslot is "Night") and not ($day is 2 and $d02Ate)>>
	<<if $player.money gte 15>>
		<<link '<span class="action-icon">🛵</span><span class="action-text">Order delivery<span class="action-sub">Somebody else cooks tonight</span></span><span class="action-cost">$15-30</span>' "Home_Kitchen_OrderDelivery">><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<div class="action-btn action-locked"><span class="action-icon">🛵</span><span class="action-text">Order delivery<span class="action-sub">Can&apos;t afford it right now</span></span></div>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

</div>

<div class="choice-block" style="margin-top:2rem;">
	<<link '<span>← Back to the apartment</span>' "Home">><</link>>
</div>

:: Home_Kitchen_OrderDelivery [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<<if $day is 2 and not $metCody>>

<<ImagePlaceholder "Delivery guy Cody at the door with a pizza box" "float" "assets/characters/supporting/cody-delivery.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>The irony isn&apos;t lost on me, a delivery person ordering delivery. I open the DashDrop app, the same one I use on the other side of the transaction, and order a pizza. Large pepperoni, $18. I tip $8 because I know exactly what it&apos;s like to carry food up three flights for someone who stiffs you.</p>

<p>Thirty minutes later, a knock at the door.</p>

<p>I open it. The delivery guy looks early twenties, dark hair, easy smile, a cap from a pizza place that&apos;s seen better days. He sees me and his expression does something subtle, a shift from &quot;delivery mode&quot; to &quot;oh, she&apos;s pretty&quot; that I&apos;ve never once been on the receiving end of before.</p>

<<Dialogue "Cody" "🍕" "Having a night in?" "">>

<p>&quot;Yeah. Thanks.&quot; I take the pizza and my fingers brush his on the box. His eyes flick down to my hand, then back up to my face. He&apos;s looking at me the way guys look at girls. I know this look. I&apos;ve done this look myself, or tried to, awkwardly, from the other side. But being inside it feels different. Being seen is nothing like seeing.</p>

<p>I close the door and lean against it. The pizza box is warm against my chest.</p>

<p>A delivery guy just smiled at me, a cute delivery guy, and some part of my brain, some traitorous little corner of it, noted that he was cute. Filed it away. Kept it.</p>

<p>I don&apos;t know what to do with that information, so I eat the pizza instead.</p>

</div>

<<SceneDivider "Phone">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I eat pizza on the couch and watch something on TV that doesn&apos;t really register. I try to feel normal. The jeans and t-shirt help, I kept them on after the thrift store. It&apos;s almost ordinary. Almost.</p>

<p>My phone buzzes. Nolan, for the third time now: &quot;seriously u good?? Can I do anything?&quot;</p>

<p>I stare at it. Three question marks. Nolan, who never uses punctuation, suddenly using three question marks. He&apos;s actually worried.</p>

</div>

<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "seriously u good?? Can I do anything?" "">>
<<Dialogue $player.name "👤" "yeah just a bug. Give me a couple days." "you">>
<<Dialogue "Nolan" "💪" "aight feel better dude 💪" "">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>Dude. He called me dude. I put the phone face-down on the couch.</p>

<p>The DashDrop app has a shift scheduled for tomorrow. I stare at the notification. I have to work. I have to go out into the world on a scooter and deliver food to strangers who&apos;ll look at me and see a woman they don&apos;t recognize, and I have to act like that&apos;s normal, because if I don&apos;t work, I don&apos;t eat, and the fact that my body changed overnight hasn&apos;t changed the basic economics of being broke.</p>

<p>Money doesn&apos;t stop being necessary just because your chromosomes rearranged themselves.</p>

<p>One more notification, an email from the university: &quot;Records update received from [legal office]. Please confirm your preferred name for academic correspondence.&quot;</p>

<p>I open it. There&apos;s a text field. Preferred name.</p>

<p>I type &quot;<<print $player.name>>.&quot; Stare at it. Delete it. Type &quot;Marcus.&quot; Stare at that too. Delete it. Type &quot;<<print $player.name>>&quot; again.</p>

<p>My finger hovers over Send. <<print $player.name>>. That&apos;s the name on my new ID now. The name NovaCure printed on the documents. The name sitting in a database somewhere, attached to my Social Security number, replacing the one my parents gave me twenty years ago.</p>

<p>I press Send.</p>

<p>The confirmation email arrives eight seconds later. &quot;Thank you, <<print $player.name>>. Your records have been updated.&quot;</p>

<p>I close the email and put the phone face-down on the couch. I eat another slice of pizza and try not to think about it. Try not to think about it at all.</p>

</div>

<div class="choice-block">
	<<link '<span>🛏️ It&apos;s getting late. Go to bed.</span>' "Home_Kitchen">>
		<<set $player.money -= 26>>
		<<set $metCody to true>>
		<<set $d02NolanTexted to true>>
		<<set $d02UniEmail to true>>
		<<set $d02Ate to true>>
		<<set $player.energy to Math.clamp($player.energy + 25, 0, 100)>>
		<<set $timeslot to "Night">>
	<</link>>
</div>

<<elseif $day is 3 and $metCody and not $metCodyD3>>

<<ImagePlaceholder "Cody at the door again, leaning in the frame, pizza box in hand" "float" "assets/characters/supporting/cody-door-d3.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I order pizza again. Same app, same place, same large pepperoni that costs $18 plus tip. I can't keep doing this, the math on delivery fees alone is going to eat through my savings faster than rent, but I don't have the energy to cook again and I just want to sit on the couch and eat pizza and pretend the world isn't real for a while.</p>

<p>Twenty-two minutes later the buzzer goes off. "Come up. 4B."</p>

<p>Footsteps on the stairs. A knock. I open the door.</p>

<p>It's Cody. Same guy from last night, mid-twenties, brown hair, delivery bag over one shoulder, DashDrop jacket unzipped over a plain white tee. He recognizes me, I can tell by the way his eyes do the quick up-down-up men do when they're cataloguing a woman's body in the half second before politeness catches up with impulse.</p>

<<Dialogue "Cody" "🍕" "Hey, night-in girl. Two nights in a row. I'm gonna start thinking you're ordering just to see me." "">>

<p>My face gets warm, heat climbing from my neck to my cheeks, and I know I'm blushing because this body does that now, broadcasts every emotion straight to the surface of my skin with zero delay.</p>

<p>"Maybe I just like the pizza," I say.</p>

<<Dialogue "Cody" "🍕" "The pizza from Sal's? That's loyalty, not love." "">>

<p>He hands me the box. His fingers brush mine during the transfer. Warm. Calloused. Working hands.</p>

<<Dialogue "Cody" "🍕" "You sure you're not just lonely on a Saturday night?" "">>

<p>"Aren't we all?"</p>

<p>He laughs, an actual laugh, not a polite exhale. "Fair point. Well, if you get tired of Sal's mediocre pepperoni, there's a Thai place on Seventh that does a green curry that'll change your life. Just saying."</p>

<p>He lingers in the doorway, not pushing, just staying, the way someone stays when they're hoping the conversation continues.</p>

<<Dialogue "Cody" "🍕" "I'm Cody, by the way. In case you wanna request me next time." "">>

<p>"Mia." The name comes out easier than it did yesterday. Smoother, like a coin that's been handled enough times to lose its sharp edges.</p>

<<Dialogue "Cody" "🍕" "Mia. Well, enjoy your mediocre pepperoni. I'll be out here in the cold if you need me." "">>

<p>He turns and walks down the stairs. I close the door and lean against it, the pizza box warming my forearms, my cheeks still burning, my heart doing something complicated in my chest that I refuse to analyze.</p>

<p>He was flirting with me. Obviously, unmistakably flirting. The kind Marcus never received and never initiated, because Marcus was invisible in the specific way average-looking men are invisible. Not ugly, not handsome, just background noise. Furniture with a delivery bag.</p>

<p>Mia is not invisible. Mia gets looked at. Mia gets a delivery boy lingering in her doorway trying to stretch a conversation that should've ended at "here's your pizza."</p>

<p>I eat a slice standing in the kitchen. The pizza is mediocre, Cody was right about that. But the warm spot in my chest stays for an hour.</p>

</div>

<<set $metCodyD3 to true>>
<<run window.rbSpend(26, "food")>>
<<run window.statChange("fem", 1)>>
<<run window.statChange("att", 1)>>

<div class="choice-block">
	<<link '<span>← Back to the kitchen</span>' "Home_Kitchen">><</link>>
</div>

<<else>>

<<set _rbCost to window.rbRandom(15, 30)>>
<<set _rbNpc to window.rbRandom(1, 3)>>

<div class="prose-block">

<<switch _rbNpc>>

<<case 1>>
<p>A young woman in a delivery jacket hands over the bag without much ceremony. &quot;Enjoy your meal.&quot; She&apos;s gone before you finish saying thanks.</p>

<<case 2>>
<p>A guy about your age, checking his phone more than he checks you, hands off the order on autopilot. &quot;Have a good one.&quot;</p>

<<case 3>>
<p>Wrong order. It happens. The delivery guy looks mortified, &quot;oh no, oh man, I am so sorry&quot;, and offers to run back for the right one. You tell him not to bother, and he leaves you a discount code out of sheer guilt.</p>

<</switch>>

</div>

<div class="choice-block">
	<<link '<span>← Back to the kitchen</span>' "Home_Kitchen">>
		<<run window.rbSpend(_rbCost, "food")>>
		<<set $player.energy to Math.clamp($player.energy + 30, 0, 100)>>
		<<set $player.stress to Math.clamp($player.stress - 3, 0, 100)>>
		<<if $day is 2>><<set $d02Ate to true>><</if>>
	<</link>>
</div>

<</if>>

:: Home_Kitchen_CookD2 [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I&apos;m going to cook something that isn&apos;t instant ramen for once. This is either growth or desperation. Possibly both at the same time.</p>

<p>Pasta, I can manage pasta. Boil water, add noodles, heat sauce from a jar. Three steps. Even this body, with its different height and different reach and different everything, should be able to handle three steps.</p>

<p>I fill the pot. The faucet is the same but my hands are smaller now and the pot feels heavier than it should. I set it on the burner and turn the gas on, the click-click-click of the igniter catching, then a blue flame.</p>

<p>While the water heats I open the sauce jar, twisting, then twisting harder. My grip strength has dropped along with the rest of my upper body mass, and the jar simply won&apos;t budge. I try running it under hot water. I try the rubber grip trick with a dishcloth. I try swearing at it directly.</p>

<p>The jar defeats me for a solid four minutes. Then the lid finally pops and marinara sauce sprays clean across my t-shirt.</p>

<p>&quot;GREAT.&quot;</p>

<p>I change shirts and add this to the running list: jar lids are apparently a gendered experience. Men open jars without thinking twice. Women develop strategies. I now need strategies of my own.</p>

<p>The pasta turns out edible, if I&apos;m being generous, slightly overcooked. The sauce comes straight from a jar and I didn&apos;t add anything to it because I honestly don&apos;t know what &quot;anything&quot; would even be. But it&apos;s warm and it&apos;s real food, and I sit at the wobbly kitchen table and eat it with a fork, the first meal I&apos;ve actually cooked and sat down for in weeks.</p>

<p>It tastes like survival, which mostly just tastes like Prego and overcooked penne. Not Michelin-star material. But mine.</p>

</div>

<div class="choice-block">
	<<link '<span>← Back to the kitchen</span>' "Home_Kitchen">>
		<<set $player.energy to Math.clamp($player.energy + 30, 0, 100)>>
		<<set $cookingSkill to 1>>
	<</link>>
</div>

:: Home_Kitchen_Breakfast [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>Breakfast is stale cereal, store brand, the kind that comes in a bag instead of a box because the bag costs $1.29, with the last of the milk. I check the expiration date. Yesterday. I smell it anyway. Fine enough. I pour a bowl and eat standing at the counter, since the single chair at my tiny table has one leg shorter than the others and I&apos;m not in the mood for wobbling this morning.</p>

<p>I check my phone while chewing.</p>

<p>Three missed calls from Pinnacle Student Loan Services, the automated kind that calls daily, sometimes twice, always from a different number so I can&apos;t block them. $23,400 in student loans. Minimum payment, $487 a month. I haven&apos;t made a payment in four months.</p>

<p>One email from Mrs. Park, subject line: <strong>FINAL NOTICE</strong>. I open it. &quot;Mr. Cole, you are $1,300 past due (2 months). Pay in full within 7 days or vacate the premises. This is not a request. M. Park.&quot; I close the email and stare at the cabinet above the stove, then open it and count the ramen packets. Eleven. That&apos;s eleven dinners. If I get evicted, I won&apos;t even have a kitchen left to boil water in.</p>

<p>One notification from the DashDrop app: &quot;Your shift starts at 11:00 AM. Tap to confirm.&quot; I tap. The gig economy doesn&apos;t care that I&apos;m drowning, it just needs me carrying food from point A to point B on an electric scooter that&apos;s one pothole away from dying completely.</p>

<p>One text from Nolan: &quot;Gym tomorrow? 💪&quot; I text back: &quot;maybe.&quot;</p>

<p>Nolan Reeves, the closest thing I&apos;ve got to a best friend, which says less about Nolan&apos;s significance and more about how isolated I actually am. We met at freshman orientation, he sat next to me and said &quot;this professor sucks, wanna get food?&quot; and that was pretty much it. Two years of gym sessions, bad movies, and the kind of male friendship where genuine emotion gets communicated exclusively through shoulder punches and the word &quot;bro.&quot;</p>

</div>

<div class="choice-block">
	<<link '<span>← Back to the kitchen</span>' "Home_Kitchen">>
		<<set $ateBreakfast to true>>
		<<set $player.energy to Math.clamp($player.energy + 8, 0, 100)>>
		<<run window.rbSendSMS("nolan", false, "Gym tomorrow? 💪")>>
	<</link>>
</div>
